description:
In 2026, Averna and Spherea joined forces to form the Spherea Group.  A global Test & Quality Solution leader, Averna Powered by Spherea partners with product designers, developers and manufacturers to help them achieve higher product quality, accelerate time to market and protect their brands by covering and offering solutions and expertise for the entire product lifecycle.


Averna Powered by Spherea offers specialized expertise and innovative test, vision inspection, precision assembly and automated solutions that deliver substantial technical, financial and market benefits for clients in the aerospace, automotive, consumer electronics, defense, energy, industrials, medical devices & life sciences, semiconductor, telecom and transportation industries.


Their solutions include prototyping & consulting, precision assembly & production, automated test solutions, in-line test systems, test system replication, and test platforms & products. Averna Powered by Spherea’s expertise ranges from vision systems, specialized battery test, RF & microwave and fiber optics to robotics & motion, instrumentation, control systems, and data management.


**Job Description**
**Position Overview**
The Account Manager role is responsible for developing top-tier accounts in India.This role blends complex technical problems, a consultative solution-based selling culture and exposure to world-renowned technology organizations we proudly call our customers. The ideal candidate will have a solid technical background in engineering fields such as mechanical, automation, electrical, or electronics, and a proven ability to develop and implement sales strategies for complex technical solutions. This highly visible, cross-functional role is a great opportunity to showcase your skills within all departments of Averna and across the globe.


**The successful candidate will:**

* Identify/ Develop New Business focusing on Test System Integration (design, replication, support) in Averna’s target industries;
* Maintain/grow existing accounts;
* Build/execute/report on account plans through collaboration with internal teams (Marketing, Operations, etc.);
* Present Solution concepts and Business proposals to our customers;
* Manage opportunities by leveraging strong relationships you build with Averna’s world-class pre-sales teams.
* Define account strategies and execute sales plan
* Manage Salesforce CRM to maintain the sales funnel, forecast sales, and generate accurate sales reports.

**Qualifications**
**The ideal candidate in a few words:**
**Education & Technical Expertise**

* Bachelor’s degree in engineering (Mechanical, Optical, Electrical preferred);
* Solid understanding of engineering design and manufacturing processes;
* Technical understanding of automation, test, and measurement equipment concepts;
* Experience with automation applications, including precision mechanics and optical systems;

**Sales & Account Management Experience**

* 5+ years of experience in custom automation solution selling, including Test & Measurement solutions for Manufacturing Industry;
* Demonstrated experience in consultative technology solution selling of capital equipment to OEMs/CMs;
* Business development of key accounts, including qualifying customers for Averna’s capabilities and driving internal teams to meet customer requirements;
* Account planning and management;
* Track record of annual sales in the millions/ year range
* Excellent communication, negotiation, and relationship-building skills.
* Familiarity with the National Instruments toolset a plus
* PLC Beckhoff based automation selling a plus

**Work Style & Logistics**

* Onsite/Hybrid work style;
* Ability to travel up to 70% of the time (travel domestically and internationally as needed).

**Additional Information**
**What's in it for YOU:**

* A dynamic sales role with direct exposure to world-class technology organizations;
* Be part of a global team with a strong and collaborative work culture;
* A highly visible, cross-functional position that highlights your expertise across all Averna departments and global markets;
* Competitive benefits package;
* Opportunities to travel ;
* Be part of a company that puts ESG at the heart of its mission, for people, planet, and performance.

Averna is committed to employment equity and to encouraging diversity and inclusion. We are pleased to consider all qualified applicants for employment, regardless of race, color, religion, sexual orientation, gender, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected status.

**Note - Candidates should have international exposure. International banking experience is a must.**

**FUNCTIONAL DUTIES**

 

·       Act as a member of Human Resources team, partner with HR Advisory team and HR centers of expertise in the Head office in Moscow. Ensure effective communication across and within the organization. Encourage good corporate citizenship and effective teamwork.

·       Manage and effectively deliver HR annual processes: budget planning, performance management, compensation planning;

·       Work closely with Head office HR to develop, implement and coordinate all the branch's overall HR processes aligned with the bank's business objectives;

·       Act as a strategic advisor to the branch management team on HR-related issues and best practices;

·       Oversee end-to-end recruitment processes to attract and hire qualified talent for all branch roles;

·       Provide and manage an effective recruitment service: resource planning, headcount/candidate approval administration, vendor management;

·       Work with local universities and Head office recruitment to manage and ensure quality graduate recruitment program. Ensure Employer Brand is appropriately marketed in all target populations;

·       Mitigate employee relations issues and risks for the organization accessing internal and external advice as necessary; 

·       Manage employment contracts for New Delhi Branch employees, control and coordinate HR related questions related to hiring, termination, sick leaves, and vacation. Ensure appropriate controls and compliance on all employee related matters e.g. taxation, regulatory compliance, employment law, and visa and border controls;

·       Stay updated on industry trends, emerging HR technologies, and regulatory changes affecting the banking sector;

·       Comply with the requirements of the legislation of Indian and local regulations and procedures of the Bank / Branch when performing labor (functional) duties;

·       Make sure all HR policies and procedures are up to date and in line with the local legislation and aligned with the Head office policies;

 

**QUALIFICATION REQUIREMENTS AND NEEDED KNOWLEDGES**

·       Work experience: not less than 10 years as HR manager/HR Business Partner

·       
Good professional ethics, integrity, characters, and reputation, having a good record of compliance with laws and regulations, and having a spotless record;

·       Fluent written and spoken English. Knowledge of Russian would be a plus;

·       Familiar with the best HR practices, policies, procedures, Indian legislation;

·       Strong communication skills: verbal, written and presentation;

·       Indian labor laws and regulations, banking industry-specific HR management practices, and the regulations of Head Office, and comply with in the daily activities.

·       Local policies, economy and their changes in order to avoid the political and market risks.

·       Working experience in banking and financial industry

**LOCATION**

New Delhi

**WORK MODE**

5 days WFO

**TITLE: Associate, Asset Management Brio India**
**DEPARTMENT:**
**Brio Asset Management**
**REPORTS TO: VP, Asset Management Brio India**
In 2025, Blackstone established Brio Real Estate (“Brio”) as a portfolio company focused on real estate credit. Brio is a specialized global commercial real estate asset services platform that manages and supports Blackstone’s Real Estate Debt Strategies business (“BREDS”) across the globe. Today, BREDS has more than $77 billion in investor capital across high yield / opportunistic real estate credit funds, a publicly traded Mortgage REIT, CMBS securities and insurance capital. Brio is a sophisticated real estate credit solutions provider that enhances value for investors and supports BREDS across key functions, including asset management, transactions, capital markets, surveillance, portfolio management and legal & compliance. Brio provides critical infrastructure and capabilities for BREDS to allow for effective investments and management of its global portfolio.


Blackstone is the world’s largest alternative asset manager with more than $1 trillion in assets under management. Blackstone’s scale, with roughly 12,700 real estate assets and over 240 portfolio companies, enables them to invest in dynamic sectors positioned for long-term growth. The firm seeks to deliver compelling returns for institutional and individual investors by building strong businesses that deliver lasting value. Blackstone’s global investment strategies focus on real estate, private equity, infrastructure, life sciences, growth equity, credit, secondaries and hedge funds.


**Job Summary**

* Execute asset management strategies to ensure sound management and risk mitigation across the global commercial real estate debt portfolio;
* Oversee the performance of all commercial real estate debt assets including assisting with monitoring loan performance, covenant compliance, capex tracking, IPD waterfall analysis, redemptions, prepayments, disposals, asset-level business plans, lease-up progress, borrower financials, quarterly loan reviews and on-going portfolio management workstreams;
* Produce portfolio-wide analytics to support strategic decision-making and identify emerging trends
* Operate with clear, consistent communication and expectation‑setting across a wide range of internal and external stakeholders, including Borrowers, Sponsors, syndicate/participant Lenders, Servicers, and other counterparties;
* Coordinating with lenders, borrowers and their respective lawyers in respect to loan redemptions, restructuring, amendments, waivers and other ad hoc requests.
* Provide competent analysis of a portfolio of loans and underlying security on a quarterly basis; including re-underwriting every quarter for internal presentation;
* Respond to requests for portfolio level due diligence and performance updates in a timely manner;
* Work with the Brio AM global team to ensure accuracy and compliance with industry standards and maintain a deep understanding of loan documents, including covenants, terms, and legal requirements;
* Ensure all documentation is up-to-date and supports effective asset management and risk mitigation.
* Problem solving when issues arise at the loan or portfolio level and proactively identify and report credit risk, market risk, and operational risk within the portfolio, develop and implement risk mitigation strategies with Brio AM team;
* Assist in preparing and present portfolio updates, performance reports, and recommendations to internal stakeholders;
* Participate in onboarding and integration of new technology solutions to enhance portfolio monitoring and analytics;
* Establish best practices, processes, and policies for loan monitoring and reporting.

**Qualifications**
**What you should have:**

* 4+ years of experience in asset management, investment management, or financial services;
* Experience working with global or large domestic corporations, and experience in a diverse team, with responsibilities including execution of functions and tasks, improving workflows to enhance collaboration, productivity, and professional growth;
* Advanced degree in finance, business, economics, or related field;
* Strong skills in Excel and familiarity with other Microsoft Office tools;
* Exceptional communication abilities, capable of simplifying concepts;
* Proven track record of excellence in processes and workstreams in a scalable, KPI-based environment;
* Strong capabilities in both internal and external relationship management;
* Independent and collaborative working style.

